# C016 reference-caption preparation — no product change

The smallest coherent correction is to preserve each admitted reference calculation, remove MoonPhaseTool's endpoint-derived alternate-sign claim, and label its unknown-time result visibly as a reference. The same bounded correction should remove unsupported clock claims from the chart's explanatory copy, share-card text and position-only previews. These are demonstrated current-output defects; this report does not certify a replacement implementation.

The inspected checkout is exact site `f803d2543ad81343b22d49326b8b46d0e2ea03a0` plus C015 Freeze2, patch SHA256 `b13527901ee962d462b0ddd2bdbc16f82763ffa8ad7486d797358b46f76fd0a4`. No C016 product edits were made. The root integrator owns the policy choice, scope allowance, generated metadata and eventual integration. C015's sealed source/evidence remain unchanged.

## Executed evidence

`probe-build.mjs` extracts the unchanged MoonPhaseTool `lookup` and illumination function using TypeScript's AST, then runs their actual time resolver, full engine and lite phase helpers with declared state/loader controls. Node 22.23.2 and actual Chrome 152.0.7977.83 ran ten finite caller cases and four three-point UTC phase-date controls. Chrome also reran the exact module after removing native Temporal: all same-browser outputs remained exactly equal. This is evidence that these current paths do not require native Temporal, not a guarantee of cross-runtime bit equality.

Four actual Preact DOM fixtures establish current caption visibility. The singleton unknown-time caption is inside a collapsed disclosure. For the London two-sign case and Khartoum noon-gap case, the caption is not mounted at all; the visible notice instead says the phase is unaffected by hours. The known-time/no-city UTC-conversion caption is also hidden in the disclosure. `browser-result.json` retains all text, requests and checks; four screenshots retain the native DOM state. These isolated fixtures deliberately replace the place selector and loader, do not load the full site theme, and do not supply all icon assets. They are behavior evidence, not design or full-page acceptance. All 22 requests were owned GETs, no external or non-GET requests occurred, there were no page errors, and every owned browser context/server was closed.

`output-probe.ts` additionally executes the actual public share-card formatting helpers, positions encoder/decoder, preview model, local OG HTML handler and Inspector SSR. `output-result.json` contains the exact strings and full returned HTML. It does not claim a network request, production preview or rendered PNG.

The first native driver attempt failed during bundling because CSS had no output path. Its original script/log are retained. The correction gave the fixture an output path and served its emitted CSS; no product change or weakened assertion was involved.

## Concrete counterexamples

* **Same local date, different reference clock:** unknown-time `2000-01-15`, `Africa/Khartoum` requests local 12:00, resolves to `2000-01-15T10:00:00.000Z`, offset +180, `dst-gap`, and actually formats as **13:00:00 local**. C014 correctly admits it as a member of the requested date. Its current Moon result is First Quarter, full angle `100.85543901591933`, illumination `0.594165840672007`, longitude `35.40995647837468` (Taurus). The endpoint inference adds Aries. A literal noon caption is false for this admitted result, while changing the reference instant would change the product's numerical behavior.
* **Date alone does not pin the phase category:** at UTC start/reference/end on 2024-01-09 the existing phase helper returns Waning Crescent / Waning Crescent / New Moon. On 2024-01-16 it returns Waxing Crescent / First Quarter / First Quarter, and on 2024-04-07 Waning Crescent / New Moon / New Moon. 2024-01-01 is a same-category control. These finite witnesses disprove the current date-alone exactness/phase-unaffected wording. They are not a complete date interval or an astronomy oracle.
* **Endpoint candidate omission persists in MoonPhaseTool:** Toronto 1919-03-31 and Juneau 1867-10-18 produce the reference Aries and Gemini respectively with no alternate sign. The separately retained C015 preparation proves actual same-local-date Pisces and Cancer members omitted by that inference. Removing the alternate calculation does not establish a singleton; the retained sign must be labeled a reference sign with its date-wide range unverified.
* **Exported clock claims are unsupported:** the Khartoum chart emits `12:00 reference · Birth time unknown`, settings beginning `12:00 reference`, and a birth-details line ending `12:00 local reference`, even while its provenance correctly prints the 10:00 UTC instant and DST gap. The positions token contains only bodies, angles, houseSystem and engineVersion; nevertheless its preview model says `12:00 reference / No houses / Tropical` and its actual OG HTML says `Sun and 12:00 reference Moon positions`. No clock can be reconstructed from that token.
* **Inspector has no clock authority:** its actual scene has engineVersion, confidence, anchor, bodies, houses, angles, aspects, signs, flags and houseSystem, but no input, UTC or zone. Its unknown-Moon SSR nevertheless prints the shared `12:00 local civil time` notice. This is an Inspector scene-contract finding; the current public `#p` receiver renders PositionsOnlyResult, not Inspector.

The existing phase **name** comes from `engine/lite.ts`; the displayed phase **angle and illumination** come from full-engine Sun/Moon longitudes. At 2024-01-16T10:30Z, the lite angle is `67.4524658327773` (Waxing Crescent), while the full angle is `67.61738889121597`. Applying the existing 67.5 category boundary diagnostically to the latter gives the adjacent category. This is a separate existing algorithm boundary. C016 must not silently substitute one calculation for the other or call the category an exact event. The same-instant known-time calculation remains unchanged.

## Policy options

1. **Moon-only correction, fourteen product source files:** change MoonPhaseTool, Chart's unknown-time phase label, six catalogs and six Moon pages. This corrects the visible tool flow but knowingly leaves its chart exports and shared previews claiming a clock that is unavailable. It must not be described as complete reference-caption correction.
2. **Recommended coherent current-result correction, twenty-three source files:** include the above, four chart/share/preview copy sources, two Explorer copy sources, and the three exact-key translation counterparts required by the existing contract. Preserve all primary numerical and wire outputs. Root separately refreshes the existing generated manifest using the unchanged generator. This addresses the actual Chart/Moon/Inspector/share/OG result surfaces found here without changing their APIs.
3. **A global no-time wording sweep:** would also touch unrelated transit, compatibility, solar-return, wallet, home/birth-chart/methodology pages and glossary. Their different computational contracts require separate review. Do not include this broad sweep mechanically in C016.

For option 2, suggested English semantics are: “Reference positions; the possible Moon signs across this date are unverified,” “Moon phase at reference time,” and a visible Moon tool qualification that its displayed sign and phase describe a reference moment and may differ at other times in the date. A no-city unknown result can explicitly identify the UTC date, while the generic Inspector/share wording must not infer any clock or zone. Known-time/no-city conversion wording is already truthful and can be shown visibly. Neither wording should promise that supplying a time pins a degree *exactly*.

Keep known-time labels/results and no-city UTC instant selection unchanged. In MoonPhaseTool, remove only private `altLon`, dayStart/dayEnd resolution and the two endpoint Moon calls; retain the first Moon/Sun calls, reference resolution, C014 refusal, lite phase call, full angle/illumination, revision fencing and result focus. Removing day endpoints also avoids unused endpoint resolutions currently performed for known time. Keep exact longitude in the disclosure; move the captured reference caption outside it so the qualification remains visible. Use the captured result caption rather than current editable fields.

## Exact proposed source scope

The machine-readable `scope-map.json` lists the exact paths and intended change, with frozen source hashes.

* `src/islands/MoonPhaseTool.tsx` and `src/islands/ChartCalculator.tsx` (only the latter's unknown-time Moon phase label).
* `src/lib/i18n/ui/{en,es,fr,it,pt,ru}.ts`: shared noTimeNotice, chartTimeHelp, placeHelpMoon, unknown reference captions, and the dedicated phase-reference label. Replace the retired Moon-only changed-sign/phase-unaffected key with the new reference phase key if root wants to retain the 420-key count; do not reuse its misleading name for unrelated semantics. Internal caption keys can also be renamed one-for-one if desired. No catalog changes have been made.
* `src/pages/moon-phase/index.astro` and `src/pages/{es,fr,it,pt,ru}/moon-phase/index.astro`: correct each shared FAQ answer (which feeds visible FAQ and JSON-LD) and the additional English date-alone paragraph. Preserve structure and interpretive framing.
* `src/lib/share-card-copy.ts`: exactly six referenceTimeNote values; `src/lib/share-card.ts`: two actual settings/provenance phrases and the inaccurate option comment. No render geometry, numeric positions, gestures, hidden-detail privacy behavior or token changes.
* `src/server/chart-preview-model.ts` and `src/server/chart-preview.ts`: only the no-angle settings/description strings. No route, parameter, headers, privacy limits, model shape or image algorithm changes. Root must explicitly admit this text-only server scope; it is not an API-contract rewrite.
* `src/islands/explorer/tour/copy.ts` and `src/islands/explorer/lens/copy.ts`: the six translations of the no-time body/note. Remove the unsupported noon assertion and the Tour's additional claim that all other planetary signs are certainly right. No Explorer component change is required for the shared Inspector notice.
* `src/strings/additions.{pt,fr,it}.mjs`: only `shareCard.referenceTimeNote`. Existing `scripts/build-i18n-additions.test.mjs` requires these runtime translation counterparts to be byte-identical to share-card-copy. They cannot be left stale. Root owns regeneration/review of `i18n-additions.md` with the existing generator, alongside the normal exact-base locale allowance. Spanish has no matching required counterpart for this key.

## Required implementation acceptance

Preserve exact same-runtime primary Moon UTC, longitude, Sun longitude, full angle, illumination and lite phase name bytes across the ten retained cases; separately record intentional removal of alternate metadata/endpoint work. Do not compare a changed full Lookup object to the old one or replace equality with tolerance. Retain known local/UTC, ordinary singleton/two-sign, Toronto, Juneau, Khartoum 13:00, skipped unknown refusal, known skipped-date policy, edit/replacement/unmount/recovery controls. C014 failures must still happen before any numerical work.

Add native visible-caption checks in six locales and actual Chart mode Moon unknown/known checks. Keep the phase-category witnesses and the lite/full-angle diagnostic separate. Verify the exact generic share-card settings/provenance, six locale time notes, clockless Inspector SSR and valid arbitrary no-angle OG tokens while retaining known-time snapshots, privacy/header/token tests and a real image-download flow.

Affected existing checks are `tests/moon-result-ownership-drive.mjs` (only removed endpoint-call expectations), `tests/local-date-reference-drive.mjs` (primary output parity versus intentionally removed samples), `tests/t17-positions-share.mjs`, `src/lib/share-card.test.ts`, `src/lib/share-card-copy.test.ts`, `src/lib/moon-certainty.test.tsx`, `src/islands/explorer/Inspector.test.tsx`, `tests/api/og-chart.test.ts`, and the unchanged additive-manifest contract. A dedicated caller/caption regression driver should carry the demonstrated cases. Update catalog count tests only if the net key count changes. Run the full affected suites, type/build checks and existing ownership/native gates; root retains full-build/capture and CI ownership.

## Explicit limits and remaining work

This proposal supplies no complete local-date interval, no verified date-wide candidate set, no phase-category coverage proof and no native-Temporal dependency. It does not change SDK receipt `reference: 'local-noon'`, which records the request convention rather than a guaranteed resulting wall clock. No receipt schema, positions wire, SDK numerical implementation, canonical Registry/Astrofolio, account data, server contract or publication changes are proposed.

The broad clock audit is retained in `clock-source-audit.log`. Separate rendered prose remains on the home page, birth-chart FAQs, methodology pages, glossary, compatibility, transit, solar-return and wallet surfaces. Their clocks and uncertainty need their own bounded policy review. Actual explicit noon timestamps in examples, source datasets, daily/today publication, date-format anchors and time-selection code are not automatically false and must not be globally replaced. The reference Sun downstream summary remains the separately recorded C015 boundary.

The preparation is executed and reviewable. No C016 implementation, independent acceptance, release, deployment or adoption is claimed.
